    "expectedRule": "Chapter 3 gravity starts upward and flips only on the first clear of tilted_gravity_switch or backup_gravity_well; every other clear leaves it alone. Display: title 重力极向, status 上浮/下沉, severity warning, no meter, targetReached false. Upward gravity scales trap damage and DC by -20% and encounter defense by +20%; downward gravity scales trap damage and DC by +20% and encounter defense by -20% (trap values rounded up). With mist_breathing as the main method every trap is seen through, so a risked trap deals max(4, floor(damage x 0.45)): tilted_gravity_switch 28 upward -> ceil(22.4) = 23 -> 10; coil_burst_trap 30 downward -> 36 -> 16; magnetic_rail_trap 34 upward -> ceil(27.2) = 28 -> 12. Run pressure stays 0% below 6 clears. Gates mine_upward_coil_lift (magnetic_rail_trap -> coil_burst_trap) and mine_upward_beast_lane need upward gravity; mine_downward_branch_lift (tilted_gravity_switch -> gravity_branch_reward) and mine_downward_dust_lift need downward gravity. A closed gate reads `仅上浮重力时通行；触发重力岔路闸或备用重力井换向。` or `仅下沉重力时通行；触发重力岔路闸或备用重力井换向。`, and the move is then not a legal destination. The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
